.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 13, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-PACK 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-pack
.Nd start, build and check a reproducibility bundle
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis pack init
.Op Fl t | Fl -template Cm plain | r | python
.Ar dir
.Nm noqtis pack build
.Fl k Ar key
.Op Fl p Ar key.pub
.Op Fl -format Cm 1 | 2
.Op Fl -lock Ar file ...
.Op Fl o Ar file
.Op Fl f
.Op Fl -no-files
.Ar dir
.Nm noqtis pack check
.Op Fl p Ar key.pub
.Ar dir | file
.Nm noqtis pack unpack
.Ar file dir
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A reproducibility bundle is a capsule
.Pq Xr noqtis-capsule 5
whose data record
.Pq Xr noqtis-data 5
holds the environment of the run and the digests of its lock files,
sealed, and shipped as one file.
Each action is a command the tool already has, run in order.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm init
Start a bundle in
.Ar dir
(made when it is not there) from a template: the folders
.Pa data/ ,
the code folder
.Pf ( Pa code/ ,
.Pa R/
or
.Pa src/ )
and
.Pa output/ ,
a
.Pa README.md
that says what goes where and how the lock file is made
.Pf ( Pa renv.lock
from
.Ql renv::snapshot() ,
.Pa uv.lock ) ,
kept when there is one, and an empty data record.
A folder with a data record is refused.
.It Cm build
Record the environment
.Po
.Xr noqtis-env 1 ;
.Fl -lock
as there
.Pc ,
seal
.Po
.Xr noqtis-seal 1 ;
.Fl k ,
.Fl p ,
.Fl -format
as there
.Pc ,
and with
.Fl o
write the bundle file
.Po
.Xr noqtis-export 1
.Fl -as Cm bundle ;
.Fl f
replaces a file there,
.Fl -no-files
leaves out every file but the data record
.Pc .
.It Cm check
Before shipping: the capsule
.Po
.Xr noqtis-check 1 ,
with
.Fl p
.Pc ,
its data record
.Po
.Xr noqtis-data 1
.Cm check :
sources, schemas, chunks, and each lock file against the digest
.Cm env
recorded
.Pc ,
and that the environment and at least one lock file are recorded.
.Ar file
is a bundle; a bundle without its files has no data to check, and
fails here.
.It Cm unpack
Read the bundle
.Ar file
into the new folder
.Ar dir
.Pq Xr nqdunpack 3 ,
refusing it whole for anything malformed, and for any path that would
leave
.Ar dir .
Check the folder after with
.Xr noqtis-check 1 .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
Done; for
.Cm check ,
every check passed.
.It 1
A check failed, or the bundle is malformed.
.It 2
A usage error, or a file or folder that cannot be read or written.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis pack init --template r study
$ noqtis data add --url https://example.org/a.csv study data/a.csv
$ noqtis pack build -k me -o study.nqb study
$ noqtis pack check -p me.pub study.nqb
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-check 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-data 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-env 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-export 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-seal 1 ,
.Xr nqdpack 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5 ,
.Xr noqtis-data 5
